{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>את לבבך ואת לבב</b> — rashei tevot: אלול. Therefore the custom to rise early for Selichot from Rosh Chodesh Elul onward. And likewise 'לולא האמנתי לראות בטוב ה׳' — לולא, letters אלול. For from Elul onward I tremble before HaShem." "<b>את לבבך ואת</b> — in gematria: this equals the days of the Messiah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The phrase 'את לבבך ואת לבב' spans the end of Deut 30:6 through the beginning of 30:7; the rashei tevot of these four words spell אלול."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:03.109636631Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}